WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.782
This is an important checkpoint.

00:00:01.782 --> 00:00:07.817
If you understand everything up to this point, you already understand the core architecture of RAG.

00:00:07.817 --> 00:00:13.772
On the indexing side, we clean documents, create chunks, and generate embeddings.

00:00:13.772 --> 00:00:18.442
On the question side, we embed the query, retrieve relevant chunks, build a prompt,

00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:22.072
and generate an answer with sources.

00:00:22.072 --> 00:00:25.917
Everything that follows is an improvement around this architecture.

00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:30.827
[tts-break] A vector database changes how vectors and metadata are stored and searched.

00:00:30.827 --> 00:00:34.312
Hybrid retrieval changes how candidates are ranked.

00:00:34.312 --> 00:00:37.662
Reranking improves the order of those candidates.

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:41.142
Evaluation tells us whether changes actually help.

00:00:41.142 --> 00:00:44.532
But the core information flow remains the same.

00:00:44.532 --> 00:00:50.177
Before continuing, make sure you could explain this pipeline without looking at the code.

00:00:50.177 --> 00:00:55.412
If you can describe each stage and why it exists, you are ready for the more practical production-oriented

00:00:55.412 --> 00:00:57.511
parts of the module.
